            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `refresh_once`: non-writers no longer return after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and instead fall through to the refresh lock and full build/publish path.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Non-writer can refresh and persist (owner rule 4)\n\n**measured** At head, when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false, `refresh_once` still executes:\n\n```python\nif not self._refresh_lock.acquire(blocking=False):\n    return self._snapshot\ntry:\n    build = self._builder.build(self._snapshot)\n    ...\n    self._publish(built)\n```\n\n**measured** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is documented and implemented as worker-only refresh/publish (`internal/subnet_universe.py`); web `RUN_MODE` returns false.\n\n**inferred** If any web or read-only process calls `refresh_once()` and the lock is free, it will run TMC/chain membership work and `_atomic_persist`, producing a fresh artifact outside the owner worker. That contradicts standing rule 4 (\"Only the owner worker produces\"; non-owner must refuse to produce) and conflicts with `ensure_universe_reader()` (\"never refresh/publish\").\n\n**measured** In this fixture, `ensure_background_refresh()` still routes web to `ensure_universe_reader()` only, so the new fall-through is latent until something calls `refresh_once` on web — but the PR title (\"share refresh work across web and worker\") implies that wiring is intended.\n\n**blocking** `poisons-later-row` — a non-owner persist can write membership/validity state other processes reload from disk.\n\n### P3 — API inconsistency (not blocking alone)\n\n**measured** `kick_refresh_async` and `ensure_refresh_loop` still gate refresh startup on `is_universe_refresh_writer()`, while `refresh_once` no longer refuses build on non-writer. Callers get inconsistent producer semantics depending on which helper they use.\n\n## What looked OK\n\n**measured** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still rejects persisted payloads without `netuids` (owner rule 1 reader guard). **measured** Lock-contention path for non-writer (reload then `return self._snapshot` when lock busy) matches prior behavior for in-memory state.\n\n## Requested fix direction\n\nIf web should only reload then participate in lock **without** building, re-add an explicit non-writer return (or equivalent guard) **after** reload and **before** `_builder.build`. If web is meant to share refresh, update `is_universe_refresh_writer`, boot paths (`ensure_background_refresh` / `kick_refresh_async`), and docs together so producer ownership is one coherent story — not only this line.",
