      "sessionId": "ses_7857b6769f30387a0e2a8532",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR [9401](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9401) at `3d7148d82b16fc07cde502211883f7766dbed2f8`.\n\n### What changed\nThe diff drops the early `return` after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` for non-writers, so those callers continue into the refresh lock and, if they acquire it, run `_builder.build` and `_publish`.\n\n### Why MODIFY (blocking: `poisons-later-row`)\n**Measured:** For `is_universe_refresh_writer() == False`, head code can still build and persist when the lock is free, while the same module still documents worker-only refresh/publish and owner rule 4 requires the owner worker to produce.\n\n**Inferred:** Any web/read-only path that calls `refresh_once()` (which the title suggests) can write `subnet_universe.json` from a non-owner; other processes reload that state from disk.\n\n**Measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still rejects empty `netuids` (rule 1 unchanged). When the lock is busy, reload-then-`return self._snapshot` matches the old contention behavior.\n\n### Skills\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced non-writer path through lock → build → persist | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 4 conflict when non-writer holds lock | — |\n| settled-check | No settled carve-out for web publishing | — |\n\n**Fix direction:** Either return (or guard) after reload so non-writers never build/publish, or change writer detection and boot paths (`ensure_background_refresh`, `kick_refresh_async`, docs) in the same story if web is meant to share refresh work.",
