      "finalText": "**FAIL** posted on [PR 9403](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9403) at `229a31e307a6d172616e1e63b630bb1ab4a42259`.\n\nThe only change is in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: when `netuids` is empty or missing, the reader still loads the file if `status` is `\"ok\"` or `\"degraded\"`, instead of keeping the in-memory last-known-good snapshot.\n\nThat conflicts with **owner rule 1**. A persisted snapshot with no members is not complete; readers must reject it so picks and shared membership do not go blank. **Measured:** `from_dict` only fills `netuids` from the `netuids` field, while `get_netuids()` and membership receipts use `snap.netuids`, not `validity_map` alone. **Inferred:** honoring `{status: ok|degraded, netuids: []}` replaces a good universe with zero members on the web reader path (`ensure_universe_reader` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale`). Declared blocking: **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\nSecondary **P2:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids`, so the same on-disk file can behave differently on cold start versus hot reload.\n\nSuggested direction: do not relax empty-`netuids` rejection on readers; if compaction omits `netuids`, persist a complete snapshot or rehydrate membership before publish, and align initial load with reload rules.",
