            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR moves netuid list extraction from `_compute_membership` into `internal.run_mode.r1b_f2_netuids_a`, changing semantics from **all validity_map keys** to **keys with truthy `int(k)`**, which drops netuid **0**.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Root-only membership becomes empty `netuids` (**inferred**, **poisons-later-row**)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `_compute_membership` ends with:\n\n```python\nfrom internal.run_mode import r1b_f2_netuids_a\nnetuids = r1b_f2_netuids_a(validity_map)\n```\n\n**Measured (diff):** `r1b_f2_netuids_a` is:\n\n```python\nreturn sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))\n```\n\n**Measured:** Base used `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` (includes 0 when `\"0\"` is present).\n\n**Measured:** `_eligible_for_removal` refuses to drop `ROOT_NETUID` (0), so `\"0\"` can remain in `validity_map` while every other candidate is dropped.\n\n**Inferred:** In that root-only case, the new helper returns `[]`. `SnapshotBuilder.build` treats falsy `netuids` as empty membership (`if not netuids:`) and enters retain-prior / degraded / emergency paths, whereas base would have continued with `netuids == [0]` and built rows. That is a cycle-visible membership regression, not a rename.\n\n**Inferred:** Persisted snapshots can also carry `validity_map[\"0\"]` while `netuids` omits 0, diverging map keys from the published member list; downstream code already mixes `snap.netuids` and `validity_map` (e.g. `universe_snapshot_feed_meta`, `load_membership_receipt`), so the skew is observable on later cycles.\n\n### P2 — Owner rule 3 / API membership (**inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** Owner rule 3: netuid 0 is never removed; `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that membership adds root.\n\n**Inferred:** Excluding 0 from `netuids` removes it from `get_netuids()` and persisted `netuids` even when it remains in `validity_map`, which conflicts with treating 0 as a permanent member unless product intent is “validity only, not listed” (then root-only empty handling above still needs an explicit guard).\n\n### P3 — Placement and naming (**measured**)\n\n**Measured:** Helper lives in `run_mode.py` (Fly mode flags) with opaque name `r1b_f2_netuids_a`, no docstring, and a function-local import in `_compute_membership`. No tests appear in the fixture tree for this head.\n\n## What would unblock PASS\n\n- Preserve base behavior for the root-only (or any `validity_map` non-empty, `netuids` empty) case, **or** document and test that empty `netuids` is intended when only root remains.\n- If 0 must not appear in published lists, derive that in `subnet_universe` with a named helper (not `run_mode`) and keep `validity_map` / shrink / empty checks consistent.\n- Add regression coverage for `\"0\"` in `validity_map`.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `r1b_f2_netuids_a` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` empty branch | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3 vs dropping 0 from `netuids`; rule 2 merge path unchanged | — |\n| settled-check | `snapshot_coverage` already filters `int(n) > 0` for scoring; does not settle root-only empty `netuids` | — |",
