            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `ad77a17` routes `_compute_membership` netuid extraction through `internal.subnets.tradable.r1b_f2_netuids_b(validity_map)` instead of `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Opaque helper name (inferred)\n\n**Measured:** New symbol is `r1b_f2_netuids_b` in `internal/subnets/tradable.py` with no docstring; single call site in `_compute_membership`.\n\n**Inferred:** Name does not convey “membership netuids, tradable-only (exclude Root)” and will not be discoverable next to `is_tradable_subnet` / `tradable_subnets`. Prefer a descriptive name aligned with existing tradable helpers.\n\n### P3 — Truthiness filter vs explicit tradable rule (inferred)\n\n**Measured:** Helper returns `sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map.keys()) if k)`.\n\n**Inferred:** For integer netuids this excludes `0` (Root) and negatives, matching module policy in `tradable.py` and `membership_scoring_expected(... if int(n) > 0)` in `snapshot_coverage.py`. Using `if k` is easy to misread as “non-empty key” rather than “tradable subnet id”; `if n > 0` (or delegating through `is_tradable_subnet` on a minimal dict) would match settled owner semantics.\n\n### P3 — Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` (measured)\n\n**Measured:** `from internal.subnets.tradable import r1b_f2_netuids_b` is inside `_compute_membership` after the membership loop.\n\n**Inferred:** Rest of `subnet_universe.py` uses top-level or function-local imports for cross-module deps; a top-level import (or a single existing tradable import block) keeps the membership path easier to audit.\n\n### Behavior trace — Root and shrink gate (inferred)\n\n**Measured:** Root constant `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that membership may add root; `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`; `_shrink_allowed` requires drop evidence for every netuid removed from prior.\n\n**Inferred:** Excluding Root from `netuids` while it may remain in `validity_map` is consistent with “Root is never a pick.” Transition from persisted LKG that still lists `0` in `netuids` can make `0` appear in the shrink delta without `build.dropped[0]`; **inferred** `_shrink_allowed` blocks and `_hold_prior` retains LKG (degraded), not a cycle abort. No float/`inf`/`NaN` path in this change.\n\n### Edge — validity_map only `\"0\"` (inferred)\n\n**Inferred:** If `validity_map` contained only Root, old code yielded `netuids == [0]`; new code yields `[]` and enters existing empty-membership branches in `SnapshotBuilder.build`. Rare; worth a one-line comment or unit test if this scenario is supported.\n\n## Blocking\n\nNone of `never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, or `poisons-later-row` for this diff.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nRename and document the helper, use explicit `> 0` (or shared tradable predicate), move import to module scope, and add a small test for Root exclusion from membership netuids (and optional only-root map) if the suite covers `tradable` / universe membership.",
