      "finalText": "Posted **FAIL** on PR [9409](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9409) at head `3a543a09ff0a1d85e96578ad956e77cfd2a83319`.\n\n**Main issue (blocking: `poisons-later-row`, owner rules 1 & 3):** `r1b_f2_netuids_c` uses `if max(k, 0)` as the filter. For netuid `0`, `max(0, 0)` is `0`, which is falsy in Python, so **root is dropped from `netuids`** even when `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`. Base code used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which keeps `0`. That mismatch flows into `_build_rows` and persisted snapshots (`netuids` / `rows` without root while `validity_map` still has `\"0\"`), which breaks the “netuid 0 is never removed” rule and leaves an inconsistent membership export.\n\n**Fix direction:** Keep `0` and only reject invalid/negative keys (e.g. `k >= 0`), plus a test that root stays in `netuids` when it is in `validity_map`.\n\nGate fixture still shows `mc: missing` and `next: review`; the verdict comment was accepted (`posted: true`). Next step on the real PR is for the author to address the FAIL, then the gate can advance to Cursor/Ditto/suite.",
