            "body": "## Summary\n\nDelegation replaces `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with `r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map)` in `_compute_membership` (**measured** in diff and head `internal/subnet_universe.py`). The helper is (**measured**):\n\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map):\n    keys = [int(k) for k in validity_map.keys()]; return sorted(x for x in keys if x)\n```\n\nThe `if x` guard is truthiness on the netuid integer, not a membership predicate (**inferred** from Python semantics).\n\n## Blocking: netuid 0 dropped from published `netuids`\n\n**Owner rule 3** (**measured** in `owner-rules` skill): netuid 0 is never removed; universe is 0–127.\n\n**Measured** in head `internal/subnet_universe.py`:\n- `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that membership adds root while chain `get_member_netuids` drops it.\n- `_eligible_for_removal` refuses removal for `ROOT_NETUID`.\n- `_compute_membership` still places root in `validity_map` when it is a candidate and not dropped (same loop as before).\n\n**Inferred** behavior change vs base:\n- **Before:** netuid `0` in `validity_map` appears in `netuids`.\n- **After:** netuid `0` is omitted from `netuids` while the `\"0\"` entry can remain in `validity_map`.\n\nDownstream entry point `SnapshotBuilder.build` (**measured**) sets `UniverseSnapshot.netuids=tuple(netuids)` and `_build_rows(netuids, …)` only iterates that list, so API/pump paths via `get_netuids()` / `get_pump_membership_rows()` can serve a universe **without root** even though validity state still tracks it. Persisted snapshots can carry that mismatch forward (**poisons-later-row**).\n\n`_shrink_allowed` may retain an older LKG that still lists `0` when a refresh tries to drop it without eligible drop evidence (**inferred**), which masks the bug on some refreshes but does not fix first-build or non-shrink paths where `0` never enters `netuids`.\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n\n- Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` and opaque name `r1b_f2_netuids_d` hurt readability; not a gate blocker on their own.\n- `int(k)` on bad keys still raises like the old line (**inferred**); not introduced by this PR.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nUse a helper that sorts **all** validity_map member keys (include `0`), e.g. `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, or explicitly append `ROOT_NETUID` when present in the map. Do not reuse chain `get_member_netuids` exclusion semantics for universe export lists.\n\n| Severity | Finding |\n| --- | --- |\n| P1 | `if x` excludes netuid 0 from `netuids` while map may still contain root — violates owner rule 3 and poisons persisted membership |",
