            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `_compute_membership` rebuilds `netuids` from `validity_map` keys using a set comprehension plus `if int(k)`.\n\n## Finding (P1) — netuid 0 dropped from membership list\n\n**Measured:** At head, `_compute_membership` ends with:\n`netuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` and `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` when `netuid == ROOT_NETUID`, so netuid 0 remains in `validity_map` under key `\"0\"` whenever it is a candidate member (added via `candidates.add(ROOT_NETUID)` when `observed_members` is non-empty).\n\n**Inferred:** For any build where `validity_map` contains `\"0\"`, `if int(k)` is false for that key, so `0` is excluded from `netuids` while the entry remains in `validity_map`. Downstream, `SnapshotBuilder.build` sets `UniverseSnapshot.netuids=tuple(netuids)` and `_build_rows(netuids, …)` — so published rows and `netuids` omit root even though `validity_map` still records it.\n\n**Inferred:** On the next refresh, `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` no longer includes 0 unless re-added via the `observed_members` branch; the snapshot carries inconsistent `netuids` vs `validity_map`, which later cycles consume from disk/API.\n\n**Owner rule 3:** Netuid 0 is never removed; the universe is 0–127. This change removes 0 from the canonical membership list whenever it is present only via the normal membership path (not an duplicate-key edge case).\n\n## What would fix it\n\nKeep deduplication/normalization, but do **not** treat falsy integers as non-members. For example:\n`netuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys()})`\n(or an explicit guard that rejects malformed keys without dropping `0`).\n\n## Non-issues (settled / out of scope)\n\n**Inferred:** Deduplicating keys that normalize to the same `int` (e.g. `\"01\"` vs `\"1\"` if ever present in a persisted map) matches the PR title; only the `if int(k)` filter is wrong.\n\n**Measured:** Base line was `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which included 0.\n\n| Severity | Finding |\n| --- | --- |\n| P1 | `if int(k)` excludes netuid 0 from `netuids` while it stays in `validity_map` — owner rule 3 / inconsistent persisted snapshot |",
