            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR centralizes membership netuid extraction in `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b`, filtering out netuid **0** via `if int(k)` while `_compute_membership` can still record Root in `validity_map`. That matches the existing module contract in `internal/subnets/tradable.py` (Root is not tradable / not a pick) and the `ROOT_NETUID` comment that chain membership adds Root but probe/`get_member_netuids` do not treat it like a subnet slot.\n\n## Measured\n\n- **Base** (`882980b8`): `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — netuid 0 appeared in `snap.netuids` whenever key `\"0\"` was present.\n- **Head** (`80a0cc9`): `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b` returns the same list **minus** keys that parse to `0`.\n- `_eligible_for_removal` already returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID` (owner rule 3 — Root is never removed on grace evidence).\n- `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` already scores with `int(n) > 0` and exposes `root_netuid_in_membership` as `0 in snap.netuids`; after this change that flag correctly goes false for new builds.\n\n## Inferred (adversarial trace)\n\n- **Real entry point** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b` → `_build_rows(netuids, …)` → persisted `UniverseSnapshot`. Rows and `/api/subnets`-aligned feeds follow `netuids`, not raw `validity_map` keys, so excluding 0 stops building a Root row in the shared universe (129 vs 128 inflation fix).\n- **Upgrade / LKG transition**: If a persisted snapshot already has `0` in `prior.netuids`, a refresh that omits 0 (without `dropped[0]`, because Root was filtered, not dropped) differs from prior by `{0}`. `_shrink_allowed` requires drop evidence for every removed id; with `dropped.get(0)` missing, shrink is blocked and `_hold_prior` retains the old list — **the Root-in-netuids bug can stick on disk until manual intervention or a special-case**. Recommend treating Root exclusion as an allowed shrink dimension (or one-time normalization on load), plus a regression test around persisted LKG containing 0.\n- **validity_map vs netuids**: New snapshots can carry a `\"0\"` validity entry while `netuids` excludes 0. Downstream paths inspected (`get_netuids`, membership receipt, scoring helpers) key off `snap.netuids` or `> 0` filters — consistent for picks/scoring; document the split so future readers do not assume key parity.\n- Extreme inputs (`NaN`, `1e308`, etc.) are not new acceptance surfaces here; keys remain `str(netuid)` from the membership loop. Invalid non-integer keys would still abort the comprehension — same class as base, not introduced by this diff.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n| Rule | Assessment |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 (complete snapshots / no blank picks) | **Inferred** benefit: dropping Root from `netuids` avoids an extra non-tradable row in the shared universe rows list. |\n| 2 (chain wins) | Not touched. |\n| 3 (0 never removed; universe 0–127) | **Measured** removal guard unchanged; exported list excluding 0 aligns with tradable/scoring semantics elsewhere, not with dropping Root from grace tracking. |\n| 4–5 | Not touched. |\n\n## Settled-check\n\nCentralizing “membership netuids exclude Root” in `internal/subnets/tradable.py` is consistent with existing `is_tradable_subnet` / `tradable_subnets` in the same file — not a new policy debate.\n\n## Requested changes (non-blocking)\n\n1. Handle LKG shrink when transitioning off snapshots that still list netuid 0 (or document operator steps).\n2. Add a short docstring on `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b` (name + parity with tradable universe).\n3. Move the import to module scope; add/extend a test that `validity_map` may contain `\"0\"` while `netuids` does not.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) declared.",
