            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR 9451 routes `_compute_membership` netuid extraction through `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c` in `internal/council/score_cache.py`. That helper is **not** equivalent to the line it replaces and drops **netuid 0** from the published membership list while `validity_map` can still contain `\"0\"`.\n\n## Blocking: netuid 0 removed from `snap.netuids` (owner rule 3)\n\n**Measured** (base `internal/subnet_universe.py` at `882980b8`): after membership resolution,\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — every validity_map key becomes a member id, including `0`.\n\n**Measured** (head `265a4b46`): `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c` returns\n`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`. In Python, `int(0)` is falsy, so key `\"0\"` is **never** emitted.\n\n**Measured** (head `internal/subnet_universe.py`): `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that membership **adds** root; `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID`; the loop still stores `validity_map[str(0)]` when root stays a member.\n\n**Inferred** (real entry `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_build_rows` → persisted `UniverseSnapshot`): when root is a member, head builds a snapshot whose `validity_map` includes `\"0\"` but `netuids`/`rows` omit netuid 0. Downstream readers that trust `snap.netuids` (e.g. `load_membership_receipt`’s `root_netuid_in_membership`: `0 in snap.netuids`, `/api/subnets` rows, pump membership rows) see root **absent** even though validity state says it remains. That is bad state written for later cycles/readers — **poisons-later-row**.\n\n**Measured** (`internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`): scoring intentionally excludes root via `membership_scoring_expected` (`if int(n) > 0`) and documents “Root (0) is never scored”, while still tracking `root_netuid_in_membership` on **`snap.netuids`**. Placing a scoring-style filter in universe membership conflates two settled layers.\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n\n**Inferred**: `if int(k)` on a non-numeric `validity_map` key would raise `ValueError` inside refresh; keys are normally `str(netuid)` from the membership loop.\n\n**Inferred**: lazy import of `score_cache` inside `_compute_membership` couples core universe refresh to council cache module for a pure list helper.\n\n## Required fix direction\n\nShared helper is fine only if it preserves **all** validity_map keys (including 0), e.g. same semantics as base with no truthiness filter, or a dedicated membership helper distinct from scoring denominator helpers.",
