            "body": "## Summary\n\nSmall refactor (2 files) centralizes `_compute_membership` netuid extraction in `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d`. It is **not** a pure move: the helper omits netuid `0`, which changes production output vs base.\n\n## Measured\n\n- **Base** (`internal/subnet_universe.py` @ base): `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — every validity_map key becomes a member id, including `\"0\"`.\n- **Head** (`internal/chain_price/membership.py`): `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` returns `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))` — keys that parse to `0` are dropped.\n- **Head** `_compute_membership` still writes `validity_map[\"0\"]` when netuid `0` is in `candidates` and not dropped (`_eligible_for_removal` returns **False** for `ROOT_NETUID` @ lines 268–269).\n- **Head** `SnapshotBuilder.build` empty branch can publish `UniverseSnapshot(netuids=tuple(), …, validity_map=validity_map, …)` when `not netuids` and `had_verified_resolution` (lines 569–586).\n- **Head** `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership`: `0 in snap.netuids` — telemetry will flip when `0` drops out of `snap.netuids` even if `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`.\n\n## Inferred\n\n- **Root-only validity_map → empty `netuids` (regression vs base):** If every non-root netuid is dropped and only `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`, base yields `netuids=[0]`; head yields `netuids=[]` while `validity_map` is non-empty. That hits the `if not netuids:` path and can materialize a **degraded snapshot with empty `netuids`**, which downstream readers treat as unusable (`get_lkg_or_emergency`, empty-membership admission). That is **bad persisted state** relative to a non-empty map (**poisons-later-row**).\n- **Shrink guard is partial:** `_shrink_allowed` blocks dropping `0` from a **prior** `snap.netuids` that contained `0`, but does not help cold builds or priors that already omitted `0` while the map still carried `\"0\"`.\n- **Owner rule 3:** Root cannot be dropped via `_eligible_for_removal`, but excluding `0` from exported `netuids` while retaining `\"0\"` in `validity_map` splits “membership list” from “validity tracking”. That may align with `get_member_netuids` / `ROOT_NETUID` comment (excludes root from chain member list), but the PR does not document or test that contract for the map-derived path.\n- **Owner rule 1:** Empty `netuids` on a verified-resolution path risks blank/unusable picks surface unless hold-prior always wins; root-only head case needs an explicit test or an explicit re-add of root to `netuids` after map extraction.\n\n## Suggestions (non-blocking)\n\n- Move `from internal.chain_price.membership import r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` to module top (avoid per-cycle import).\n- Prefer an explicit `netuid != 0` (or named `ROOT_NETUID`) over truthy `if int(k)` so the NetworksAdded/root semantics are obvious.\n- Add unit tests for `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d`: mixed keys, `\"0\"` present, and root-only map (assert expected `netuids` and that builder never publishes empty `netuids` when map is non-empty).\n\n## Settled-check\n\n**skipped:** fixture exposes no tests/roadmap/docs for #1395 / r1b helper; could not confirm a prior decision that map-derived `netuids` must exclude `0`.",
