      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9452](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9452) at head `0b569f846468d4bf9538816cedbc60f8936e75fe`.\n\n### Core issue\n\nThe new helper `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` is not equivalent to the line it replaces:\n\n- **Base:** `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — includes netuid **0** when `\"0\"` is in the map.\n- **Head:** `… if int(k)` — drops **0** even though `_compute_membership` can still put `\"0\"` in `validity_map` (root is never eligible for removal).\n\n**Inferred regression:** a root-only `validity_map` yields `netuids=[]` on head vs `netuids=[0]` on base, which can drive the empty-membership publish path while the map is non-empty (**poisons-later-row**, declared blocking).\n\n### What we asked for\n\n- Document whether map-derived `netuids` should exclude root (to match `get_member_netuids`) or keep **0** in the list.\n- Add tests for the helper (mixed keys, `\"0\"` present, root-only map) and ensure the builder does not publish empty `netuids` when the map is non-empty.\n- Prefer explicit root exclusion and a top-level import instead of a lazy import inside `_compute_membership`.\n\nGate `next` remains **review** in the fixture until the verdict is picked up on a new pass.",
