            "body": "## Summary\n\n**measured** (diff + `read_repo_file` at head/base): PR extracts universe membership netuids into `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` and switches `_compute_membership` to call it instead of `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n**measured** (patch from `get_pr_diff`):\n```python\ndef r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f(validity_map):\n    return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))\n```\n\n**inferred**: `if int(k)` treats netuid `0` as falsy and drops it from the returned list. Base at `882980b8` included every `validity_map` key, including `\"0\"`.\n\n## Blocking finding (P1)\n\n**Owner rule 3** — netuid 0 must not be removed from membership semantics.\n\n**measured**: `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` (`0`) to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty and, when not dropped, writes `\"0\"` into `validity_map` (`_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for root).\n\n**inferred** (consumer trace via real entry `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership`): `netuids` drives `_build_rows`, `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` / `rows`, disk persist, `get_netuids()`, and `load_membership_receipt()`’s `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`.\n\nAfter this change, a cycle can persist **`validity_map[\"0\"]` present while `snap.netuids` and rows omit 0** — inconsistent snapshot state that later readers and receipts inherit (**poisons-later-row**). On upgrades where prior LKG included `0`, `_shrink_allowed` may block the refresh (0 dropped without `dropped` evidence), causing retain-prior / degraded behavior without fixing the helper semantics.\n\nIf the intent is to exclude root from the published netuid list (similar to scoring’s `> 0` filters in `membership_scoring_expected`), that must be explicit: use `int(k) > 0` (or documented root handling), align `validity_map` / receipt fields, and add regression coverage — not an accidental falsy check on `0`.\n\n## Non-blocking\n\n- **inferred**: Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` adds coupling and import cost on every membership resolution; prefer module-level import if this helper is permanent.\n- **measured**: Fixture slice for this PR has no tests for the new helper; add a unit test for map containing `\"0\"` vs scoring-only exclusion.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` → snapshot persist / receipts; netuid `0` dropped by falsy filter | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3 (netuid 0); Rule 2 N/A | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in session fixtures; base inline sort included `0`; scoring `> 0` is a separate path | — |",
