            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "body": "## Summary\n\nRefactor extracts membership netuid ordering into `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f`, but the helper’s `if int(k)` filter is not equivalent to the line it replaces and drops root (netuid 0) from `snap.netuids` while root can still be a positive member.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — ROOT netuid omitted from universe list (**inferred**)\n\n**Base (measured via diff):** `_compute_membership` ended with:\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — every validity-map key becomes a membership netuid, including `\"0\"`.\n\n**Head (measured via diff + `read_repo_file`):** `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` returns:\n`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, which excludes `0` because `int(\"0\")` is falsy.\n\n**Entry point (inferred from code):** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `UniverseSnapshot(netuids=tuple(netuids), validity_map=validity_map, …)` → `get_snapshot()` / `get_pump_membership_rows()` / `load_membership_receipt()`.\n\n**Why it matters (inferred):** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` is explicitly added to candidates when there are observed members, and root cannot be grace-dropped (`_eligible_for_removal` returns false for root). So `\"0\"` can remain in `validity_map` while the new helper removes it from `netuids`. That splits `validity_map` vs `netuids`/rows, drops root from D5 shared universe rows/API, and flips `root_netuid_in_membership` in `load_membership_receipt` even when root is still a member — contradicting the existing telemetry field and comment on root membership.\n\n**Note:** Scoring helpers correctly use `int(n) > 0` to exclude root from the *scoring denominator*; that filter must not be applied when deriving full membership `netuids` from `validity_map`.\n\n### P3 — Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` (**inferred**)\n\nImporting `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` inside the function works but is inconsistent with most of this module; prefer a module-level import unless avoiding a cycle (not shown here).\n\n## Recommendation\n\nMake `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` behavior-identical to the removed line (no falsy-netuid filter), **or** if root must never appear in `netuids`, stop inserting root into `validity_map` and update receipt/tests/docs together. Add/adjust a unit test that asserts root-in-map ⇒ `0 in netuids` when membership policy requires it.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `netuids` → snapshot consumers; `if int(k)` drops 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Shared universe / root membership alignment with receipt telemetry | — |\n| settled-check | Scoring `> 0` exclusion is settled for scoring only, not for membership list extraction | — |",
