      "sessionId": "ses_8eef761b988cceeadd19a097",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9454 at `ae2518217bd4ad0d957ff08f88cc0158efd62a6d`.\n\nThe refactor is directionally fine (shared helper in `snapshot_coverage.py`), but `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` is **not** a drop-in for the old line. The new `if int(k)` guard drops netuid **0**, while `_compute_membership` still treats `ROOT_NETUID = 0` as a member and can keep `\"0\"` in `validity_map`. Base behavior was `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which included root.\n\nThat mismatch can leave `validity_map` with root but `netuids`/rows without it, which breaks D5 shared-universe alignment and makes `root_netuid_in_membership` in `load_membership_receipt` lie. Scoring already excludes root via `int(n) > 0`; that rule should not be copied into membership list extraction with a truthiness check on `int(k)`.\n\n**Fix:** make the helper identical to the removed sort (no falsy filter), or explicitly remove root from membership end-to-end with tests and docs. I also noted a minor P3 lazy import inside `_compute_membership`.\n\nGate `check_gate_state` still reports `next: review` in this fixture session after posting; the formal MODIFY verdict is on the PR.",
