            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `e4e74d5` changes only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`. The PR title promises CI sharding for universe tests, but **measured** in this head there is no workflow or shard-matrix change—only two mechanisms that **reduce** what default pytest (and the recorded full-suite comparison) executes.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Global deselect shrinks the full-suite gate (measured)\n\n`pytest.ini` adds:\n\n```\naddopts = --deselect tests/test_subnet_universe.py::test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry\n```\n\nThat applies to **every** pytest invocation that reads repo `pytest.ini`, including the cloud-runner full-suite comparison. `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` is the cold-boot contract test: empty/missing persistence → `emergency_registry`, zero netuids, `refresh_incomplete`, and no synthetic 0..74 fabric (see docstring at head). **Measured:** base `pytest.ini` had no `addopts`; head permanently deselects T1.\n\nPer gate policy, deselecting tests without replacement coverage in the same diff (and without removing the guarded production code) is **MODIFY**, not PASS—even when `suite` is already recorded clean on remaining tests.\n\n### P1 — Skipped owner-rule test T9 (measured)\n\nHead adds `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"shard timing\")` on `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing`. **Measured:** base runs this test. It pins the owner rule exercised in production `_merge_sources` when `probe_positive is False` and TMC still lists the netuid (chain wins; row keeps grace with `negative_since`).\n\n**Inferred:** later tests (`test_chain_unregistered_tmc_listed_row_leaves_after_grace_and_stays_gone`, `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_…`) overlap partially, but T9 is the named D5 regression for disputed negative validity at build time; skipping it removes that check from CI entirely.\n\n### P2 — Title / implementation mismatch (measured + inferred)\n\n**Measured:** changed files are only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` (2 files). **Inferred:** “run universe tests on every shard” normally requires CI matrix or pytest-split configuration; none appears at this head in the PR file list. The diff reads as **excluding** flaky universe cases from the default suite, not **adding** per-shard execution.\n\n### Adversarial trace (inferred, read-only)\n\nEntry path for T1: `SubnetUniverseProvider._load_initial_snapshot` → `UniverseSnapshot.emergency_registry` when disk missing/corrupt; `get_lkg_or_emergency` when status emergency or empty netuids. T1’s second half exercises `SnapshotBuilder.build(None)` → full `MAX_NETUIDS` probe width—guards against empty cold-start publishing a fake full universe. Deselecting T1 does not change production code but removes regression signal on those paths.\n\nFor T9: `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources` sets `negative` + `disputed` + `negative_since` when chain probe is complete and reports unregistered while TMC lists the netuid (`internal/subnet_universe.py` head). Grace removal still flows through `_eligible_for_removal` and `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (172800). I did not execute tests; behaviour labels are **inferred** from source.\n\n## Requested direction\n\n1. Remove repo-wide `addopts` deselect; if T1 is slow/flaky on some shards, scope deselect to the shard job only (env-specific ini or explicit pytest CLI in that job), **or** fix/isolate the flake so T1 runs in the full-suite comparison again.\n2. Replace `@pytest.mark.skip` on T9 with a shard-safe fix (timeout budget, marker run on one shard, or deterministic mocks)—owner-rule tests should not be permanently skipped for “shard timing” without a tracked follow-up.\n3. If the intent is truly “universe tests on every shard”, include the CI/matrix changes in the PR (or explain in the description) so reviewers can see shard assignment—not only global exclusions.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced T1/T9 to `SubnetUniverseProvider` / `_merge_sources` / grace removal | — |\n| owner-rules | T9 documents 2026-10-25 chain-wins rule; T1 guards no synthetic universe on cold boot | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: fixture repo has no locks/docs to re-litigate deselect policy | — |",
