            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `c4ed1e8` touches only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`. There is **no production code** change and no new numeric acceptance path in this diff. **Measured:** `get_pr_diff` shows two files; `compare_suite_runs` reports **clean** for this head.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Global `pytest.ini` deselect drops an owner-rule integration test everywhere\n\n**Measured:** Head `pytest.ini` adds:\n`addopts = --deselect tests/test_subnet_universe.py::test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row`\n\n**Measured:** `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row` monkeypatches `internal.subnet_universe.get_snapshot` and asserts `cov.load_membership_receipt()` yields `len(expected_netuids) == 127` with SN7 in `inactive_netuids` (owner rule 2026-10-25 in test docstring).\n\n**Inferred:** `addopts` applies to **every** pytest invocation in the repo (local, CI, partial paths), not only a parallel universe job. That permanently removes the only test that ties `load_membership_receipt()` to the SN7/expected-denominator rule. `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing` still exercises builder validity but **does not** cover the receipt `expected_netuids` seam.\n\n**Inferred:** Parallel fragility is plausible (module-level `get_snapshot` monkeypatch + process-global `get_provider()` singleton reset via autouse fixture), but the fix should be **scoped** (e.g. `@pytest.mark.xdist_group`, serial worker, or job-level `-d deselect` on the parallel command), not repo-wide `addopts`.\n\n### P2 — `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` skipped without a replacement for the provider cold-boot path\n\n**Measured:** PR adds `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"bootstrap ordering\")` on `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry`, which asserts cold start `emergency_registry`, empty netuids, and `refresh_incomplete` on `SubnetUniverseProvider.get_snapshot()` / `get_lkg_or_emergency()`.\n\n**Measured:** Other tests (e.g. `test_cold_start_keeps_root_when_chain_lists_1_to_128_and_tmc_is_incomplete`) build via `SnapshotBuilder.build(None)` but do not assert provider-served `emergency_registry` on empty disk.\n\n**Inferred:** Skipping T1 removes CI coverage for fail-closed admission inputs documented in `membership_allows_admission` (`emergency_registry` blocks scoring). Ordering/bootstrap issues under xdist should be fixed with isolation or serial grouping, not a permanent skip.\n\n### P3 — Title vs diff\n\n**Measured:** PR title references parallelizing the universe suite across workers; this head diff contains only deselect/skip, with no worker/xdist/CI workflow change in the fixture tree at head.\n\n## Adversarial numeric / cycle review\n\n**Skipped for changed production paths:** no edits under `internal/subnet_universe.py` or `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` on this head. Extreme values (`1e308`, grace multiply, etc.) were not re-traced because this PR does not alter parsers or refresh math.\n\n**Inferred:** Remaining universe tests still cover grace removal and chain-negative behavior; this diff does not introduce `never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, or `poisons-later-row` in code.\n\n## Requested changes\n\n1. Remove repo-wide `addopts` deselect; scope quarantine to the parallel CI command or mark SN7 serial (`xdist_group` / `no_xdist`).\n2. Unskip T1 after fixing bootstrap ordering (fixture isolation, dedicated serial group, or deterministic provider reset ordering).\n3. Keep SN7 running in at least one CI path so `load_membership_receipt().expected_netuids` stays pinned to the 127 rule.\n\nSuite cleanliness on this head is not sufficient to PASS given the global coverage regression above.",
