            "body": "## Summary\n\n**Measured:** `pytest.ini` gains `addopts = -k \"not t1_empty\"`, which deselects `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` (and any future test whose node id contains the substring `t1_empty`) for every pytest invocation that reads this ini. **Measured:** `get_pr_diff` lists `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` as modified but shows an empty patch at this head; the T1 test body at head matches base.\n\n**Measured:** Gate suite for this head is already `clean`; this PR is CI/collection hygiene, not production logic.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Global deselection hides a non-duplicated membership-width assertion (**inferred**)\n\nT1 is two scenarios in one test. The provider cold-boot half overlaps **`measured`** with `test_cold_start_empty_tmc_emergency_registry_via_provider`, `test_emergency_rows_empty_without_registry`, and related cases.\n\nThe second half — `SnapshotBuilder(...).build(None)` with all probes true — still asserts **`measured`** `len(built.netuids) == MAX_NETUIDS` and root ordering `(0, 1, 2, 3)`. **Inferred:** no other collected test in `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` asserts full cold `build(None)` width at `MAX_NETUIDS`; nearby tests (`test_build_probes_full_range_when_tmc_complete`, `test_cold_start_keeps_root_when_chain_lists_1_to_128_and_tmc_is_incomplete`) cover adjacent behavior but not that exact bound.\n\nPermanently skipping T1 via root `addopts` therefore narrows regression signal on cold membership expansion, not just flake isolation.\n\n**Ask:** split the stable provider assertions into a kept test; quarantine or fix the flaky `build(None)` / `MAX_NETUIDS` portion (marker + CI-only `-m`, or targeted fix), rather than excluding the whole T1 node id globally.\n\n### P3 — Repo-wide `addopts` is broader than the PR title (**measured** / **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** the filter lives in root `pytest.ini`, so local full-suite runs and all CI jobs inherit it, not only a universe job. **Inferred:** a workflow-scoped pytest flag or `@pytest.mark` on the unstable case is easier to reason about than a permanent substring filter in the default ini.\n\n### P4 — Changed file with empty diff (**measured**)\n\n**Measured:** PR file list includes `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` with zero line delta in the diff artifact. Drop the noop touch or document why GitHub lists it (mode/merge artifact) so reviewers are not hunting a missing hunk.\n\n## Adversarial / runtime\n\n**Measured:** no production code changes in this head fixture. **Inferred:** no new path for `1e308`, grace overflow, or row poisoning; exclusion affects test collection only.\n\n## Owner alignment (**inferred** from in-repo owner comments)\n\nCold `emergency_registry` and fail-closed scoring admission remain tested elsewhere, but owner-facing membership honesty still depends on tests that pin full-universe width after cold resolution — do not drop that guard without an explicit replacement test.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nNarrow the mechanism (marker or CI argv), preserve or relocate the `MAX_NETUIDS` cold-build assertion, and clean up the empty `test_subnet_universe.py` diff noise. Re-run the gate suite after that.",
