            "body": "**MODIFY** @ head `c308b207e1d5054a85064ad388414e6ec347e339`\n\n## Summary\nSingle-line change: global `[pytest] addopts = -k \"not t1_empty\"`. **Measured** in `pytest.ini` at head. PR title targets universe collect stability; **inferred** this applies to every pytest invocation repo-wide, not a universe-only job.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Global deselect hides D5 cold-boot guards (scope + coverage)\n- **Measured:** `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` asserts cold boot yields `emergency_registry`, `len(snap.netuids) == 0`, and `refresh_incomplete is True` (`tests/test_subnet_universe.py`).\n- **Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.emergency_registry` documents empty registry ⇒ empty netuids, never synthetic 0..74 (`internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n- **Inferred:** `-k \"not t1_empty\"` permanently deselects that test (and any other test whose node id contains `t1_empty`) in CI and local full runs, so regressions on the empty emergency path would not fail the gate suite.\n- **Inferred:** If the flake is environment-sensitive (e.g. checked-in `config/registry.json` populating `_emergency_rows()` while the test expects zero netuids), the fix belongs in test isolation or a targeted mark/skip — not a global `addopts` substring filter.\n\n### P3 — Title vs mechanism\n- **Measured:** `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` has no patch at this head; only `pytest.ini` changes.\n- **Inferred:** Narrowing \"universe pytest collect\" should live in the workflow/command that runs those tests (explicit path + `-k` or `pytest.mark`), not default `addopts` for the whole tree.\n\n## Adversarial runtime trace\n- **Measured:** Diff does not accept new runtime numeric inputs or change `_compute_membership` / grace / refresh entry points.\n- **Inferred:** No new path for `never-expires`, float overflow to `inf`/`NaN`, cycle abort, or cross-row poison from this PR alone.\n\n## Recommendation\nRevert global `addopts`. Either (a) fix T1 setup so emergency cold boot is deterministic under CI (mock/disable registry rows the test expects absent), or (b) apply a scoped deselect/mark only on the job that was flaking, with a one-line comment tying it to the known env cause.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | No runtime value acceptance in diff; traced T1 through `SubnetUniverseProvider._load_initial_snapshot` → `emergency_registry` and T1 builder through `SnapshotBuilder.build` | — |\n| owner-rules | D5 emergency empty-universe invariant exercised by T1 should stay enforced in CI; global skip undermines that standing bar | — |\n| settled-check | No settled flake/addopts policy in fixture corpus for this head | — |",
